SWEET surface scan (patch 0160, boot-arg sweetsurfscan=SEC, default off; G-11 icons): every SEC seconds (80 rounds, only changes logged) log how much of every small surface (<= 1200x1200, single plane, <= 4 MiB) holds data (sampled nonzero 32-bit words) to see whether CoreAnimation's 180x180 icon render targets are ever written. Counts client lock / write-unlock traps per surface id and the last locker process (0160c); read-only (kernel mapping of an IOBufferMemoryDescriptor); no hardware access.
